\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces BFM empirical diagnostic curves with upper-tail zoom: marginal vs.\ cumulative representativeness ratios for Chile (2017 and 2022). Raw density ratio $\tilde  {\theta }(y)$ per fractal bin (gray dots), antitonic isotonic regression $\hat  {\theta }(y)$ (blue line with squares), and cumulative ratio $\hat  {\Theta }(y)$ (red line with circles). The main axes display the overall trajectory across the upper distribution ($P \ge 75\%$). The inset axes zoom in on the extreme right tail ($P \ge 98\%$), clearly resolving the crossing of $\hat  {\theta }(y)$ and $\hat  {\Theta }(y)$ at the endogenous merging point $y^*$ (marked by the dashed gray vertical line and labeled percentile). Panel (e) depicts commercial year 2017 ($y^* = 68.03$~M CLP/year, $P99.40$, 111 observations above $y^*$); Panel (f) depicts commercial year 2022 ($y^* = 190.0$~M CLP/year, $P99.90$, 12 observations above $y^*$).}}{27}{figure.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bfm-theta-Theta}{{14}{27}{BFM empirical diagnostic curves with upper-tail zoom: marginal vs.\ cumulative representativeness ratios for Chile (2017 and 2022). Raw density ratio $\tilde {\theta }(y)$ per fractal bin (gray dots), antitonic isotonic regression $\hat {\theta }(y)$ (blue line with squares), and cumulative ratio $\hat {\Theta }(y)$ (red line with circles). The main axes display the overall trajectory across the upper distribution ($P \ge 75\%$). The inset axes zoom in on the extreme right tail ($P \ge 98\%$), clearly resolving the crossing of $\hat {\theta }(y)$ and $\hat {\Theta }(y)$ at the endogenous merging point $y^*$ (marked by the dashed gray vertical line and labeled percentile). Panel (e) depicts commercial year 2017 ($y^* = 68.03$~M CLP/year, $P99.40$, 111 observations above $y^*$); Panel (f) depicts commercial year 2022 ($y^* = 190.0$~M CLP/year, $P99.90$, 12 observations above $y^*$)}{figure.14}{}}
